# .unstarted-rows — OPTIONAL. Copy to the root of the repository that owns your
# ordered backlog, alongside .ceo-todos and .row-currency.
#
# YOU PROBABLY DO NOT NEED THIS FILE. The unstarted-row sweep is switched on by
# the queue record simply EXISTING at the default path (RICH-TODOs.md, beside
# the .ceo-todos declaration). This file exists to move that path, or to narrow
# which warrant states count as work somebody could pick up now.
#
# WHAT THE SWEEP DOES
# -------------------
# At EVERY turn end — not at a land — it reads both halves of the queue and
# reports any row that names nobody as blocking it and has no live worktree
# working on it. Writing work down is not starting it, and the moment work is
# created is the moment somebody NOTICES it, which is a reporting turn rather
# than a landing.
#
# HOW A ROW GOES QUIET, and there are only two ways
# -------------------------------------------------
#   1. IT NAMES WHAT IT IS WAITING ON.
#        in the queue table   the `Blocked by` cell: anything but "—"
#        in the working record  `**Blocked:** the CEO — his billing account`
#                               in the row's prose, BEFORE its `**State:**`
#                               warrant (which is the row-currency contract's
#                               and is not disturbed by this)
#   2. A LIVE WORKTREE CLAIMS IT.
#        a branch or directory containing `row-<id>`  (row-11, row-3.1,
#        row-3-1), bounded on both sides so `row-1` never claims row 11;
#        or the id on its own line in <worktree>/.claude/row-claims.txt
#
# A row that is neither is reported BY NAME, once, and again whenever the set
# changes. Nothing blocks; nothing is killed on a timer.
#
# CHECK IT BY HAND (the same code the hook runs):
#   ~/.claude/richos-engine/scripts/unstarted-rows-lint.sh /path/to/this/repo
#   exit 0 all accounted for · 1 something is unstarted · 2 nothing was read

# Where the ordered backlog lives, repository-relative. Only needed when it is
# not RICH-TODOs.md.
QUEUE_RECORD="RICH-TODOs.md"

# Which of the working record's warrant tokens describe work somebody could
# pick up now. The vocabulary itself is declared once, in .row-currency, and is
# not repeated here — this key only SELECTS from it.
#
# BLOCKED-ON-RICH is deliberately absent from the default, and that is a
# judgment rather than an oversight: by the record's own contract it means
# "not yet prepared for the CEO", which is arguably the most unstarted state
# there is — but it is also the token used for work that has been consciously
# parked. Widening the set is one word here.
ACTIONABLE_TOKENS="OPEN BUILT BOUNDED"
